<title>UK: LME copper firms before Third Wednesday to $2,300.</title>
<headline>LME copper firms before Third Wednesday to $2,300.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Firmer, testing interim resistance at $2,300 ahead of Third Wednesday pricing. Last at $2,301/$2,305, versus $2,284 on Friday's kerb close. But LME stocks up 2,075 tonnes.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Also higher, nearing $1,600 resistance.</p>
<p>ZINC - Probing recent 6-3/4 year highs around $1,495. Stocks up 300 tonnes. OTHERS - Little changed from Friday's close.</p>
</text>
